        "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued August 11 at 8:35AM AKDT by NWS Juneau AK",
        "description": "The latest camera imagery and water level data from inside the basin\nshowed a slight drop in water level and this is indicating that\nwater has started to flow over the top of the ice dam a short time\nago. Now is the time to finalize your flood preparation for\npotential flooding impacts along the Mendenhall Lake and River.\n\nIn the past it has taken up to 6 days for a release to start. The\nNWS will continue to monitor the situation and provide updates as\nneeded including updating this statement wi",
